<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112402" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρυ-άσσομαι</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρυ-άττομαι</span></b> , prop. of spirited,
		high-fed horses, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>neigh, whinny
				and prance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Lav.Pall.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.201
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thom.
			</span></i> Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.381R.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. πρὸς τοὺς ἀγῶνας</span>
			<i>neigh eagerly</i> for the race, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				22
			</span></i>; also of a cock, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				7.7
			</span></i>, cf. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. of
			men, <i>to be wanton, haughty, insolent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.151
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				297
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ γαῦρα φρυάσσου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.33
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.180
			</span></i>: also c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρωτες σκῦλα φρυασσόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					4.215
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἐπί τινι</span>
			<i>to be proud</i> of a thing, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.74
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					4.3.27
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> trans., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταπλήττω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				1081
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρυάσσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ps.</u>
					2.1
				</span></i>
			 (quoted in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				4.25
			</span></i>); of birds, <i><span class="en">
				Cyran.
				81
			</span></i>, cf. <u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
